# Build outputs and fuzzing state — regenerated, never committed.
target
corpus
artifacts
coverage

# Fuzz dependencies are FETCHED from crates.io against the committed Cargo.lock, not vendored (see
# .cargo/config.toml). A local `cargo vendor` here would drop a large third-party tree into a public
# repository for a build that never ships, so the directory is ignored to keep that out of history.
# This is the one crate in the repo that is not vendored; ../vendor and
# ../bindings/flutter/rust/vendor stay committed, because those DO build shipped artifacts.
vendor
